  "limitations": [
    "All 32 worlds are public synthetic and exposed; no independent owner-held original science was accessed",
    "Active mediator readout is a purpose-built new observable, and the known 2-of-4 content cardinality is given equally to both models. It breaks CB3 observational role symmetry by adding information, not by extracting absent information from the old passive trace.",
    "Source-private feature locations and law formula are in the evaluator file, not imported by models. Both arm algorithms know the mechanism-probe semantics.",
    "Paired public readouts are reset to a common baseline and charged as one synthetic probe; physical reset/operation costs of a real world are not independently measured.",
    "Four-feature set was first learned using original CB3 universal 38-bit basis; source behavior lies within its broad Boolean hypothesis class. No novel operator invention or full eight-way native policy.",
    "Scored 128 new contexts per world are evaluator-only binary target choices; not an independent multi-step closed-loop world return.",
    "Source dataset training is a seeded shared action tape, not an exploration policy learned by the candidate.",
    "Candidate and strongest conventional exact same-information control have identical action/role accuracy and probe count: no algorithmic superiority.",
    "Per-world short probe SHA prefixes accompany an overall full 256-bit canonical digest; reproducible complete 88KB JSON output is generated by the pinned scorer."
  ]
}
